Subject: ashmem_memfd: include <string.h> for strcmp and memset

The file calls strcmp() and memset() without including <string.h>.
Older compilers accepted the implicit declarations with a warning; clang 21,
which ships with Android NDK r29, rejects them as an error under the C99+
rules ("ISO C99 and later do not support implicit function declarations").

This matters beyond the build failure: an implicitly declared function is
assumed to return int, so the pointer returned by memset() would be truncated
to 32 bits on arm64.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92)
Scope: adds one include; no behavioural change.

--- a/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c
+++ b/src/extension/ashmem_memfd/ashmem_memfd.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+#include <string.h>       /* strcmp, memset  */
 #include <sys/syscall.h>  /* __NR_memfd_create,  */
 #include <linux/ashmem.h> /* ASHMEM_GET_SIZE,  */
 #include <linux/memfd.h>  /* MFD_CLOEXEC  */
